---
description: Carry out the requested program inspection, execution or signed-result work using current native evidence.
args:
  goal: string
returns: ProgramRunReport
---
Work toward the user's goal using the current owned program catalog and actual compiler, callable and retained-output evidence. The runtime namespace exposes exact native discovery, inspection, revision-bound sample execution, output readback and signing; the reviewer hierarchy interprets those observations. The sibling selection and continuation judgments can help distinguish the relevant program, authorized inputs and requested signature.

Own the semantic composition: decide which evidence is needed, whether the request is inspection-only or requires execution, and how to continue after an actual result. Match purpose and scope as well as names; an archived or unrelated program is not a substitute. A compiled callable is not an executed result. Execute only authorized inputs on an actually inspected current revision, retain the real independently read receipts, and distinguish real null output from missing output. Use actual feedback to reconsider stale or interrupted work within the native grant. Do not broaden inputs after an unchecked or mismatched result, or turn a successful requested result into extra trials.

Return the actual ProgramRunReport. An unavailable program or native binding returns its supported unresolved reason. For reviewed work include only actual output receipts and a real signature when specifically requested, currently authorized and independently verified. Do not discard useful native output merely because a later signature is unavailable.
